# ============================================================================
# AISC HS Grade 9 Biology — .gitignore
# ============================================================================

# ---- OS / editor cruft ----
.DS_Store
*~
*.swp
*.swo
Thumbs.db

# ---- Local tooling state ----
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---- Logs / temp ----
*.log
*.tmp

# ---- Environment files (defensive — no .env exists today, blocks future accidents) ----
.env
.env.*

# ============================================================================
# Excluded student work — DO NOT TRACK
#
# These folders contain prior-year materials with student names in filenames
# (e.g., "Trevor S Cell Membranes...docx"). The repo is public, so excluding
# them protects student privacy (FERPA-style concern). They remain on the
# local machine; they just don't get committed or pushed.
#
# To audit what's excluded:
#   git status --ignored | grep "Prior Year Materials\|Unit 1 - Cell Biology"
# ============================================================================

**/Prior Year Materials/
HS G9 Bio Unit 2 Cell Biology (25-6)/Unit 1 - Cell Biology/

# ============================================================================
# Excluded authoring source — DO NOT TRACK
#
# The README says this repo holds only the public-facing site and the
# student-facing interactives, and that the unit plans, decks and assessments
# live in Drive and Google Classroom. That was true only because nobody had
# run `git add -A`. These folders are sitting in the working tree right now,
# and they include the Unit 3 summative paper, all three checkpoints, every
# mark scheme, the marking slip, both student lab sheets and the teacher prep
# sheet. The repo is public and Vercel deploys the whole of it, so one
# `git add -A` would put a live exam paper and its mark scheme on the internet.
#
# To audit what's excluded:
#   git status --ignored | grep "HS G9 Bio Unit"
#
# To track one deliberately, if you ever want to:
#   git add -f "<path>"
# ============================================================================

HS G9 Bio Unit */
